+# init: empty blocks ('{ }'): your code mixes both forms (2 on two lines, 1 on one line), so both are allowed. To choose on two lines: change the next line to stylebro_allow_empty_single_line_blocks = false.
+stylebro_allow_empty_single_line_blocks = true
+# init: block-bodied properties/methods: your code mixes both forms (20 on several lines, 25 on one line), so BRO1509 is off. To choose one: set dotnet_diagnostic.BRO1509.severity and remove the next line.
+dotnet_diagnostic.BRO1509.severity = none
+# init: statements after a block's '}': your code mixes both forms (94 after a blank line, 35 right below the '}'), so BRO1519 is off. To choose one: set dotnet_diagnostic.BRO1519.severity and remove the next line.
+dotnet_diagnostic.BRO1519.severity = none
+# init: nested ifs BRO1149 would merge: kept, because your code has some (4 nested ifs; any 3 keep them: BRO1149 would merge each), so BRO1149 is off. To turn it on: remove the next line.
+dotnet_diagnostic.BRO1149.severity = none
+# init: doc comment texts: your code mixes both forms (4 ending with a period, 4 without a period), so BRO1603 is off. To choose one: set dotnet_diagnostic.BRO1603.severity and remove the next line.
+dotnet_diagnostic.BRO1603.severity = none
+# init: using directives: 148 of 151 files sorted, 113 of 113 with System first
+dotnet_sort_system_directives_first = true
+# init: private constants/static readonly fields: your code mixes their casing (7 PascalCase, 12 camelCase), so BRO1306 is off (it checks constants, static readonly and non-private fields). To choose one: set stylebro_private_static_field_naming (PascalCase, camelCase, _camelCase or s_camelCase) and remove the next line.
+dotnet_diagnostic.BRO1306.severity = none
